Chitala N1.6 (native/spike/README.md): on the qemu_virt_aarch64_gicv3 board,
seL4 no longer traps a guest's WFI and WFE. seL4 passes each trap to the
guest's VMM, and libvmm (0.2.0, and upstream as of 2026-10-07) answers it by
resuming the guest, so an idle guest trapped without end through its VMM,
at the VMM's priority: millions of traps in one N1.6 run.

--- a/build_sdk.py
+++ b/build_sdk.py
@@ -321,6 +321,10 @@
             "KernelPlatform": "qemu-arm-virt",
             "QEMU_MEMORY": "2048",
             "QEMU_GIC_VERSION": 3,
+            # Chitala N1.6: a guest's WFI/WFE run on the CPU instead of trapping
+            # to its VMM, which only resumes the guest: an idle guest would
+            # otherwise trap without end through its VMM.
+            "KernelArmDisableWFIWFETraps": True,
             # There is no peripheral timer, so we use the ARM
             # architectural timer
             "KernelArmExportPTMRUser": True,
